# Development scaffolding — must never ship with the skill.
#
# Note on scope: the skill itself tells agents to exclude session artifacts via
# `git rev-parse --git-path info/exclude`, precisely so an agent never edits a
# tracked file. This .gitignore is the maintainer-side counterpart — a deliberate,
# shared policy about what may enter the distribution — and is meant to be committed.
#
# Patterns are kept narrow on purpose: a blanket `.claude/` or `.cursor/` would
# silently swallow a future maintainer's intentional shared config.

# Independent-review tool state, one-off plan exports and run scripts
.codex-verify/

# Host hook experiments; local-only settings overrides
.cursor/hooks/
.cursor/hooks.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Test installs of this skill into a host root inside the repo
.cursor/skills/
.claude/skills/
.agents/skills/

# Disabled / backup copies of any config
*.off
*.bak

# Build output. The .skill archive is derived from know-your-unknowns/ by
# scripts/build_skill.py; committing it would let the binary drift from source.
# Releases attach a copy built from the tagged commit.
dist/

# Discovery artifacts this skill's own techniques produce.
# Anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored `implementation-notes.md` also
# matches know-your-unknowns/references/implementation-notes.md, which is a
# published part of the skill -- ripgrep and friends would silently skip it.
/design-directions/
/unknowns-artifacts/
/change-report.html
/implementation-notes.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
